Oh, shoot.

737
00:48:37,682 --> 00:48:41,186
- [drawer opens]
- [objects clattering]

738
00:48:47,092 --> 00:48:48,259
Hello?

739
00:48:54,832 --> 00:48:55,832
Sera?

740
00:49:02,640 --> 00:49:05,810
[suspenseful music continues]

741
00:49:43,648 --> 00:49:46,817
[suspenseful music continues]

742
00:50:16,614 --> 00:50:18,616
Oh, what the hell, John?

743
00:50:38,469 --> 00:50:41,639
[suspenseful music continues]

744
00:50:54,485 --> 00:50:57,322
[breathing heavily]

745
00:51:08,966 --> 00:51:09,967
[thuds]

746
00:51:22,547 --> 00:51:25,049
[grunts, sighs]

747
00:51:25,850 --> 00:51:27,318
[door thuds]

748
00:51:38,763 --> 00:51:39,897
[sighs]

749
00:51:43,100 --> 00:51:46,470
What the hell is wrong with you? All
you had to do was just stay away.

750
00:51:46,471 --> 00:51:47,771
[John over phone]
<i>Yeah, I know I messed up.</i>

751
00:51:47,772 --> 00:51:49,573
<i>I messed up.
I thought I could fix it.</i>

752
00:51:49,574 --> 00:51:52,376
Just ever since we moved into the
house, everything has gone to shit.

753
00:51:52,377 --> 00:51:54,745
Listen to me.
You only have one option.

754
00:51:55,313 --> 00:51:56,346
Let it play out.

755
00:51:56,347 --> 00:51:57,882
[sighs]

756
00:52:03,321 --> 00:52:04,521
John? You still there?

757
00:52:04,522 --> 00:52:06,723
She just left my house.

758
00:52:06,724 --> 00:52:08,692
- <i>Who?</i>
- Alyssa. She just left my fucking house.

759
00:52:08,693 --> 00:52:10,360
- <i>Don't do something stupid.</i>
- [keys jingling]

760
00:52:10,361 --> 00:52:11,428
[tires screech]

761
00:52:11,429 --> 00:52:12,962
<i>Hello? John?</i>

762
00:52:12,963 --> 00:52:14,031
<i>John?</i>

763
00:52:14,965 --> 00:52:17,635
[action music plays]

764
00:52:30,615 --> 00:52:32,882
Come on, come on, come on.

765
00:52:32,883 --> 00:52:34,419
[music ends]

766
00:52:45,230 --> 00:52:48,599
[somber music plays]

767
00:52:51,969 --> 00:52:54,003
[engine stops]

768
00:52:54,004 --> 00:52:55,506
[exhales]

769
00:52:57,174 --> 00:52:58,175
[car alarm chirps]

770
00:53:08,319 --> 00:53:09,386
[door closes]

771
00:53:09,387 --> 00:53:12,923
[piano music plays]

772
00:53:35,045 --> 00:53:36,046
Where were you?

773
00:53:37,715 --> 00:53:39,549
I was running. I told you.

774
00:53:39,550 --> 00:53:41,752
For four hours? [sniffles]

775
00:53:43,321 --> 00:53:45,823
[sighs] What's wrong?

776
00:53:56,367 --> 00:53:57,668
I'm pregnant.

777
00:54:02,072 --> 00:54:03,072
Are you serious?

778
00:54:04,542 --> 00:54:06,076
- [chuckles]
- Oh, my God.

779
00:54:08,379 --> 00:54:10,247
- [John exhales]
- [Sera sniffles]

780
00:54:13,250 --> 00:54:14,752
There's something else.

781
00:54:23,661 --> 00:54:26,497
- I didn't go in the cellar.
- No, but you tried.

782
00:54:27,965 --> 00:54:30,935
Yeah, I did. I did.
That-that was stupid. I'm sorry.

783
00:54:31,769 --> 00:54:35,873
We made a promise
to each other, John. Right?

784
00:54:37,875 --> 00:54:39,944
Look, I need to know
that we're in this together.

785
00:54:41,379 --> 00:54:42,813
That I can trust you.

786
00:54:43,781 --> 00:54:45,282
It's not just us anymore.

787
00:54:46,551 --> 00:54:47,818
[sighs]

788
00:55:00,365 --> 00:55:01,532
[hammer thuds]

789
00:55:11,241 --> 00:55:14,745
[dramatic music plays]

790
00:55:35,132 --> 00:55:36,500
[music ends]

791
00:55:36,501 --> 00:55:38,702
[birds chirping]

792
00:55:38,703 --> 00:55:40,670
[Sera] Okay. So, on the left,

793
00:55:40,671 --> 00:55:44,040
there's more of like a deeper,
sagey green.

794
00:55:44,041 --> 00:55:47,111
And then on the right, it's-it's
like minty. It's lighter.

795
00:55:48,245 --> 00:55:49,246
Which one do you prefer?

796
00:55:50,214 --> 00:55:53,417
Oh. Uh... [chuckles]

797
00:55:53,418 --> 00:55:55,084
Uh, no, I like them both. Um...

798
00:55:55,085 --> 00:55:57,521
- Okay.
- Probably the one on the right.

799
00:55:57,522 --> 00:55:58,822
Yes! Okay, good.

800
00:55:58,823 --> 00:56:01,458
- Um, so, crib over here.
- Yeah.

801
00:56:01,459 --> 00:56:03,593
- Yeah.
- And then changing table,

802
00:56:03,594 --> 00:56:05,562
rocking chair right there.

803
00:56:05,563 --> 00:56:07,031
- [John] Mm-hmm.
- What?

804
00:56:08,365 --> 00:56:09,499
What?

805
00:56:09,500 --> 00:56:12,235
[inhales deeply]
Uh, I don't know.

806
00:56:12,236 --> 00:56:15,439
This-this feels a bit early.

807
00:56:15,440 --> 00:56:16,973
- Is it too early for all this?
- No.

808
00:56:16,974 --> 00:56:20,077
- You sure?
- Yes, I'm sure.

809
00:56:21,145 --> 00:56:23,880
I love you for worrying,
but it's all good.

810
00:56:23,881 --> 00:56:25,349
I'm stronger than I look.

811
00:56:27,485 --> 00:56:28,719
We're gonna be good.

812
00:56:29,454 --> 00:56:30,487
[cell phone vibrating]

813
00:56:30,488 --> 00:56:31,822
Okay.

814
00:56:34,191 --> 00:56:35,191
Work.

815
00:56:39,196 --> 00:56:40,296
Yeah? This is John.

816
00:56:40,297 --> 00:56:41,698
[over phone]
<i>Yes, it's Mrs. Taylor from HR.</i>

817
00:56:41,699 --> 00:56:43,533
- Yeah?
- <i>I wanted to inform you,</i>

818
00:56:43,534 --> 00:56:45,869
- <i>you've been cleared in the investigation.</i>
- [relieved sigh]

819
00:56:45,870 --> 00:56:47,471
- Are you serious?
- <i>Yes.</i>

820
00:56:47,472 --> 00:56:48,972
- <i>Are you able to start on Monday?</i>
- [chuckles] Okay.

821
00:56:48,973 --> 00:56:50,974
- Yes, absolutely, yes.
- <i>Okay.</i>

822
00:56:50,975 --> 00:56:52,977
Of course. Thank you. Um...

823
00:56:53,711 --> 00:56:54,979
I'll see you Monday.

824
00:56:56,481 --> 00:56:57,648
Okay.

825
00:56:59,517 --> 00:57:00,517
[sighs]

826
00:57:02,853 --> 00:57:04,021
Sorry about that.

827
00:57:04,589 --> 00:57:05,955
- All okay?
- Yeah, all good.

828
00:57:05,956 --> 00:57:08,725
Just some drama at work,
but all good now.

829
00:57:08,726 --> 00:57:10,059
Oh, okay.

830
00:57:10,060 --> 00:57:12,963
- Um, will you hold this on that side?
- Sure.

831
00:57:13,631 --> 00:57:14,932
Thank you.

832
00:57:16,033 --> 00:57:18,502
[loud drilling in distance]

833
00:57:18,503 --> 00:57:22,071
- Hey, hey. Welcome back, my man.
[chuckles] - [John] Thank you.

834
00:57:22,072 --> 00:57:23,106
There he is.

835
00:57:23,107 --> 00:57:24,440
- Good to see you.
- Yeah.

836
00:57:24,441 --> 00:57:26,743
Listen, what'd I tell you?
Trust the process.

837
00:57:26,744 --> 00:57:28,778
I don't know.
I still don't really believe it.

838
00:57:28,779 --> 00:57:30,947
Yeah, well, apparently,

839
00:57:30,948 --> 00:57:33,883
Alyssa's infatuation with you
was an open secret.

840
00:57:33,884 --> 00:57:36,153
- No one bought her sob story.
- [sneers]

841
00:57:37,187 --> 00:57:38,822
Have you-have you seen her yet?

842
00:57:38,823 --> 00:57:40,023
- No.
- No?

843
00:57:40,024 --> 00:57:42,526
- No, she was out all last week.
- Right.

844
00:57:42,527 --> 00:57:44,994
- "Self-care," they say.
- Right.

845
00:57:44,995 --> 00:57:46,896
I know HR tried to reach her
over the weekend,

846
00:57:46,897 --> 00:57:49,198
but she's-she's ducking
their calls.

847
00:57:49,199 --> 00:57:51,768
I'm guessing she caught wind
of their decision.

848
00:57:51,769 --> 00:57:53,603
But you know who is back?

849
00:57:53,604 --> 00:57:55,404
- You, rock star.
- Me.

850
00:57:55,405 --> 00:57:56,940
- Lunch is on me.
- Okay.

851
00:57:56,941 --> 00:57:58,575
Okay? And we can pretend all
this bullshit never happened.

852
00:57:58,576 --> 00:58:01,645
- Please.
- All right. Until then, get back to work.

853
00:58:01,646 --> 00:58:02,947
- Okay.
- All right.

854
00:58:08,318 --> 00:58:10,186
[John] <i>You think Emmett's gonna
care if we toss his painting?</i>

855
00:58:10,187 --> 00:58:12,356
[Sera]
Uh, remove the painting, please.

856
00:58:12,890 --> 00:58:14,058
[John] Okay.

857
00:58:18,462 --> 00:58:19,462
[Sera] What?

858
00:58:20,097 --> 00:58:21,398
What the hell is that?

859
00:58:22,633 --> 00:58:24,134
[John] Mmm.

860
00:58:36,346 --> 00:58:37,381
[Sera] What is it?

861
00:58:46,791 --> 00:58:47,958
Jesus.

862
00:58:50,494 --> 00:58:52,629
- You're overreacting.
- I'm overreacting?

863
00:58:52,630 --> 00:58:55,599
- Yes.
- We just found a bullet hole in our wall.

864
00:58:55,600 --> 00:58:57,366
Why would we not call
the police?

865
00:58:57,367 --> 00:58:59,903
Because there's probably
a rational explanation

866
00:58:59,904 --> 00:59:02,739
that doesn't require
you going nuclear, John.

867
00:59:02,740 --> 00:59:04,174
Seriously.

868
00:59:05,676 --> 00:59:07,711
Hear me out, okay?
Just hear me out.

869
00:59:07,712 --> 00:59:10,513
I have heard
that Emmett's wife and daughter,

870
00:59:10,514 --> 00:59:11,848
they left him 25 years ago.

871
00:59:11,849 --> 00:59:14,183
No one has seen them since.
No one.

872
00:59:14,184 --> 00:59:15,719
That doesn't strike you as odd?

873
00:59:15,720 --> 00:59:18,087
So you think
that he murdered them

874
00:59:18,088 --> 00:59:20,090
and they're buried
in our basement?

875
00:59:21,558 --> 00:59:22,992
Yes, I think it's possible.

876
00:59:22,993 --> 00:59:26,195
Well, don't you think the police
would have investigated?

877
00:59:26,196 --> 00:59:29,065
- I don't know.
- You-you've gotta drop this.

878
00:59:29,066 --> 00:59:30,399
You know, I'm not doing this.

879
00:59:30,400 --> 00:59:31,835
I'm not going down
the rabbit hole with you.

880
00:59:31,836 --> 00:59:33,169
This is what you do.

881
00:59:33,170 --> 00:59:34,437
- This is what I do? What do I do?
- Yes.

882
00:59:34,438 --> 00:59:36,505
Instead of seeking
rational explanations,

883
00:59:36,506 --> 00:59:38,041
you-you leap to conclusions.

884
00:59:38,042 --> 00:59:41,178
And-and most of the time,
it's fine because I love you.

885
00:59:41,879 --> 00:59:43,579
But I can't do this.

886
00:59:43,580 --> 00:59:46,100
The next eight months are gonna
be stressful enough, so please...

887
00:59:48,919 --> 00:59:50,821
Please just drop it.

888
01:00:01,098 --> 01:00:03,433
Okay. It's dropped.

889
01:00:04,835 --> 01:00:06,036
It's dropped.

890
01:00:10,507 --> 01:00:11,842
[sighs]

891
01:00:15,045 --> 01:00:18,548
[soft music plays]

892
01:00:45,075 --> 01:00:47,576
Two steps forward, one step back.
You know how it is.

893
01:00:47,577 --> 01:00:49,046
Yeah, that's how that goes.

894
01:00:49,847 --> 01:00:51,981
- [Steven] Uh, hey, Kiah.
- [Kiah] Yeah.

895
01:00:51,982 --> 01:00:53,817
What's going on?

896
01:00:53,818 --> 01:00:55,452
- You haven't heard?
- No.

897
01:00:56,086 --> 01:00:59,823
They found Alyssa's car
abandoned somewhere upstate.

898
01:00:59,824 --> 01:01:01,992
They think
she may have committed suicide.

899
01:01:02,727 --> 01:01:05,229
[indistinct chatter]

900
01:01:10,701 --> 01:01:12,936
[Kathryn] I fell asleep
on the ferry ride home.

901
01:01:12,937 --> 01:01:14,971
- [Sera] No.
- [chuckles] I did.

902
01:01:14,972 --> 01:01:18,808
If it wasn't for some guy who woke
me up, I'd probably end up in Canada.

903
01:01:18,809 --> 01:01:20,410
[Kathryn laughs]

904
01:01:22,146 --> 01:01:24,413
Okay, I've-I've been meaning
to ask you something.

905
01:01:24,414 --> 01:01:27,851
Um, when we first met,
you-you said something.

906
01:01:27,852 --> 01:01:29,986
Oh, boy. Me and my big mouth.

907
01:01:29,987 --> 01:01:31,287
I hope I didn't say anything
too offensive.

908
01:01:31,288 --> 01:01:32,756
No, no, no. It's the opposite.

909
01:01:32,757 --> 01:01:36,460
You-you actually said, "I-I hope
you guys stick around."

910
01:01:37,928 --> 01:01:39,429
- Oh.
- What'd you mean by that?

911
01:01:41,498 --> 01:01:45,269
Just that we didn't wanna lose you
guys, you know, like the others. I...

912
01:01:45,936 --> 01:01:47,804
What do you mean?
What-what others?

913
01:01:47,805 --> 01:01:49,238
The other families.

914
01:01:49,239 --> 01:01:51,240
You know, there's been
a handful of 'em over the years.

915
01:01:51,241 --> 01:01:53,209
The MacManuses
were the last ones.

916
01:01:53,210 --> 01:01:54,878
Super nice couple.

917
01:01:54,879 --> 01:01:56,946
Oh, fun, fun, fun.

918
01:01:56,947 --> 01:01:59,983
And then one day,
they were just gone.

919
01:01:59,984 --> 01:02:02,752
No goodbye. No nothing.

920
01:02:02,753 --> 01:02:05,855
- Although, [whispers] I suspected marital trouble.
- Oh.

921
01:02:05,856 --> 01:02:09,358
- I did. But you two seem happy as clams.
- [chuckles]

922
01:02:09,359 --> 01:02:13,429
And I get such a kick running
into John on my daily runs.

923
01:02:13,430 --> 01:02:17,200
Oh, my God, he must love
working from home. Oh!

924
01:02:17,201 --> 01:02:19,168
- Mm.
- I'm sorry?

925
01:02:19,169 --> 01:02:21,304
We cross paths
running around lunch,

926
01:02:21,305 --> 01:02:23,440
but I haven't seen him
in the last few weeks.

927
01:02:24,041 --> 01:02:25,209
Huh.

928
01:02:26,210 --> 01:02:28,245
[ominous music plays]

929
01:02:30,280 --> 01:02:31,715
[muffled]
Is everything all right?

930
01:02:40,324 --> 01:02:42,292
[in normal voice]
Is something going on with John?

931
01:02:43,393 --> 01:02:45,061
Uh, no.

932
01:02:45,062 --> 01:02:47,430
No, no. I, uh... I'm sorry.

933
01:02:47,431 --> 01:02:50,399
I-I... I didn't realize
how much John was running.

934
01:02:50,400 --> 01:02:52,368
Oh. [gasps]

935
01:02:52,369 --> 01:02:54,437
- It's my yoga instructor.
- Okay.

936
01:02:54,438 --> 01:02:57,306
- And he is so fucking hot.
- [both laugh]

937
01:02:57,307 --> 01:02:58,374
- I'll be right back.
- Okay.

938
01:02:58,375 --> 01:02:59,575
I'm gonna go namaste him.

939
01:02:59,576 --> 01:03:03,413
[Kathryn laughs]
So good to see you here.

940
01:03:07,918 --> 01:03:11,088
[ominous music continues]

941
01:03:19,596 --> 01:03:20,630
[music fades]

942
01:03:31,441 --> 01:03:33,076
I heard about
that girl you work with.

943
01:03:33,077 --> 01:03:35,112
The news said she was missing.

944
01:03:36,480 --> 01:03:37,513
Yeah.

945
01:03:37,514 --> 01:03:39,416
Yeah, we just found out
about it today.

946
01:03:40,851 --> 01:03:42,586
It's terrible. [sighs]

947
01:03:44,654 --> 01:03:46,423
Do the police know
what happened?

948
01:03:47,424 --> 01:03:48,893
No, I don't think so. I mean...

949
01:03:49,659 --> 01:03:53,429
they talked to some people today,
and no one seems to know much.

950
01:03:53,430 --> 01:03:55,865
Yeah, we're hoping she's okay.

951
01:03:55,866 --> 01:03:58,468
Yeah. I bet.

952
01:04:04,909 --> 01:04:07,243
[water running]

953
01:04:07,244 --> 01:04:10,447
[suspenseful music playing]

954
01:04:33,570 --> 01:04:35,439
[suspenseful music intensifies]

955
01:04:39,176 --> 01:04:40,176
[sighs]

956
01:04:40,177 --> 01:04:41,878
[music fades]

957
01:04:46,516 --> 01:04:48,352
[sighs]

958
01:04:55,092 --> 01:04:58,595
[light piano music plays]

959
01:05:10,140 --> 01:05:11,341
[objects jingle]

960
01:05:13,510 --> 01:05:14,510
[sighs]

961
01:05:26,423 --> 01:05:29,993
It's the same bullet, Sera.
It's an exact match.

962
01:05:29,994 --> 01:05:31,160
That doesn't worry you?

963
01:05:31,161 --> 01:05:32,895
Uh, okay,
so it's-it's the same brand.

964
01:05:32,896 --> 01:05:34,563
That doesn't mean
that Emmett murdered his family

965
01:05:34,564 --> 01:05:36,300
or that they're buried
in the basement.

966
01:05:36,933 --> 01:05:39,169
Yeah, but it's pretty damn
compelling, don't you think?

967
01:05:40,037 --> 01:05:42,938
Why would he just leave it in plain sight?
That makes no sense.

968
01:05:42,939 --> 01:05:45,542
I don't know. I don't know.

969
01:05:50,214 --> 01:05:51,714
- Let's look.
- Fine. You wanna look?

970
01:05:51,715 --> 01:05:53,716
- Yeah, why not? Let's look.
- Why?

971
01:05:53,717 --> 01:05:55,718
Because we'd lose
the house, John.

972
01:05:55,719 --> 01:05:58,588
We would lose everything.
Do you really want that?

973
01:05:59,789 --> 01:06:01,291
[doorbell rings]

974
01:06:04,661 --> 01:06:06,095
[Sera sighs]

975
01:06:06,096 --> 01:06:07,931
[sighs]

976
01:06:11,001 --> 01:06:12,202
Mrs. Winter?

977
01:06:13,470 --> 01:06:15,405
I'm Detective Stark.
This is Detective Weiland.

978
01:06:16,606 --> 01:06:19,376
We'd like to speak
with your husband. Is he home?

979
01:06:21,511 --> 01:06:24,080
Yeah. Uh, hi, I-I'm John Winter.
How can I help you?

980
01:06:24,081 --> 01:06:26,982
We'd like to ask you a few
questions, if you don't mind.

981
01:06:26,983 --> 01:06:29,386
Yeah, of course. Come on in.

982
01:06:30,954 --> 01:06:31,955
Please.

983
01:06:34,991 --> 01:06:35,991
Uh...

984
01:06:38,128 --> 01:06:39,296
Please.

985
01:06:39,896 --> 01:06:40,896
In here.

986
01:06:52,709 --> 01:06:55,678
Can I get you anything?
A coffee? Water? Tea?

987
01:06:55,679 --> 01:06:57,580
No, ma'am, we're fine.
Thank you.

988
01:06:57,581 --> 01:07:00,384
If you don't mind, we'd prefer
to speak with your husband alone.

989
01:07:02,552 --> 01:07:04,688
Oh. Uh, yeah, of course.

990
01:07:20,137 --> 01:07:21,470
What's this about?

991
01:07:21,471 --> 01:07:23,339
[Stark] Looking into
a missing persons report.

992
01:07:23,340 --> 01:07:25,040
Do you know Alyssa Hayes?

993
01:07:25,041 --> 01:07:26,910
[John] Of course.
We work at the same company.

994
01:07:27,711 --> 01:07:29,678
[Stark] A friend reported
her missing last week.

995
01:07:29,679 --> 01:07:32,348
- [John clears throat] - We found her
car, but we're still trying to locate her.

996
01:07:32,349 --> 01:07:34,617
We understand
Miss Hayes recently filed

997
01:07:34,618 --> 01:07:36,852
a sexual harassment claim
against you.

998
01:07:36,853 --> 01:07:37,853
Yeah.

999
01:07:39,823 --> 01:07:43,992
We dated a-a while back,
and, uh, when I broke it off,

1000
01:07:43,993 --> 01:07:46,562
she had trouble moving on,
especially after I met Sera.

1001
01:07:46,563 --> 01:07:49,965
Last fall,
she made a pass at me,

1002
01:07:49,966 --> 01:07:51,967
and I turned her down.

1003
01:07:51,968 --> 01:07:54,069
And, uh, after that, she made up
all this stuff about me.

1004
01:07:54,070 --> 01:07:58,308
The company did an investigation,
and I was-I was cleared.

1005
01:07:59,309 --> 01:08:03,011
[Weiland] Did you have any contact with
Miss Hayes during the investigation?

1006
01:08:03,012 --> 01:08:05,013
I did. I-I... I did.

1007
01:08:05,014 --> 01:08:09,486
I, uh, called her, like, a week or
two ago, and I left a voicemail.

1008
01:08:10,654 --> 01:08:12,921
[Stark] What about the call
on March 18th?

1009
01:08:12,922 --> 01:08:13,922
[John sighs]

1010
01:08:13,923 --> 01:08:15,958
I don't know. I'm sorry.
I-I don't know.

1011
01:08:15,959 --> 01:08:18,127
According to Miss Hayes's
cell phone records,

1012
01:08:18,128 --> 01:08:21,364
you spoke with her during
the morning hours of March 18th.

1013
01:08:21,365 --> 01:08:22,599
Is that correct?

1014
01:08:24,067 --> 01:08:26,703
Sure, yeah. I wanted
to straighten things out.

1015
01:08:28,505 --> 01:08:30,073
It was a 30-second call.

1016
01:08:31,541 --> 01:08:33,810
I can't imagine
how much was straightened out.

1017
01:08:34,544 --> 01:08:37,746
Yeah, that's true. We, uh,
agreed to meet in person.

1018
01:08:37,747 --> 01:08:40,384
[Stark] And did you?
Meet in person?

1019
01:08:41,218 --> 01:08:45,354
I mean, you haven't been
in the office for five weeks, correct?

1020
01:08:45,355 --> 01:08:47,991
- So you had plenty of time.
- [John exhales]

1021
01:08:48,925 --> 01:08:49,726
Yeah.

1022
01:08:49,727 --> 01:08:51,527
Alyssa drove up, and we-we met

1023
01:08:51,528 --> 01:08:53,596
in a nearby
underground parking garage.

1024
01:08:53,597 --> 01:08:56,232
[Stark] And this is Saturday,
March 18th?

1025
01:08:56,233 --> 01:08:57,900
That's what it says, yes.

1026
01:08:57,901 --> 01:08:58,902
[Weiland] What time?

1027
01:09:00,837 --> 01:09:01,871
2:00 p.m.

1028
01:09:03,840 --> 01:09:05,641
Walk us through
your conversation.

1029
01:09:05,642 --> 01:09:07,410
[John] No, like I said,
I just wanted to talk to her.

1030
01:09:07,411 --> 01:09:11,915
I wanted to let her know how this was
impacting my life, my career. Uh...

1031
01:09:12,882 --> 01:09:15,451
At one point, she agreed
to drop the allegations

1032
01:09:15,452 --> 01:09:16,952
if I went back with her.

1033
01:09:16,953 --> 01:09:21,524
I-I refused, and she got
very upset, and she drove off.

1034
01:09:21,525 --> 01:09:24,227
[Weiland] Was that the last time
you saw her?

1035
01:09:24,228 --> 01:09:25,429
Yes.

1036
01:09:27,764 --> 01:09:29,798
According to phone records,
her cell pinged a tower

1037
01:09:29,799 --> 01:09:31,901
in this neighborhood
the following day.

1038
01:09:32,869 --> 01:09:36,440
Like I said, the last time I
saw her was when she drove off.

1039
01:09:37,207 --> 01:09:38,674
[Weiland] What about you?

1040
01:09:38,675 --> 01:09:40,710
Where were you on March 19th?

1041
01:09:42,346 --> 01:09:43,879
I'm sorry.
Am I-am I a suspect here?

1042
01:09:43,880 --> 01:09:46,249
- [Stark] It's a simple question, Mr. Winter.
- Okay.

1043
01:09:46,250 --> 01:09:50,519
Where were you during the
afternoon hours of March 19th?

1044
01:09:50,520 --> 01:09:52,622
Here. I was here.

1045
01:09:53,423 --> 01:09:55,559
Can anyone corroborate this?

1046
01:09:58,428 --> 01:10:00,563
[tense music intensifies]

1047
01:10:00,564 --> 01:10:03,065
Yep. Yes.

1048
01:10:03,066 --> 01:10:04,500
I was with him.

1049
01:10:04,501 --> 01:10:09,405
We recently found out we're
pregnant, so, um, he was home.

1050
01:10:09,406 --> 01:10:11,608
We're just finishing up
some house projects.

1051
01:10:14,544 --> 01:10:15,779
Congratulations.

1052
01:10:25,489 --> 01:10:26,690
We'll be in touch.

1053
01:10:37,501 --> 01:10:39,168
[John exhales]

1054
01:10:42,339 --> 01:10:43,507
- Sera...
- Don't.

1055
01:10:44,708 --> 01:10:47,776
I didn't tell you about the
allegations because they weren't true.

1056
01:10:47,777 --> 01:10:50,012
So you continued to lie

1057
01:10:50,013 --> 01:10:54,883
by pretending to go to work
for a month.

1058
01:10:54,884 --> 01:10:57,354
Oh, God, yeah.
That was stupid. I'm sorry.

1059
01:10:58,455 --> 01:11:01,625
Why don't you tell me the real
reason you kept it a secret?

1060
01:11:02,626 --> 01:11:04,092
What do you mean?

1061
01:11:04,093 --> 01:11:06,896
Remember the company party
right after we got engaged?

1062
01:11:07,864 --> 01:11:09,366
I had to leave early.

1063
01:11:10,233 --> 01:11:14,937
When you came home, you
smelled like sex and jasmine.

1064
01:11:14,938 --> 01:11:15,805
It's jasmine.

1065
01:11:15,806 --> 01:11:17,040
<i>It's my favorite.</i>

1066
01:11:25,315 --> 01:11:28,917
I chose to look the other way
because I-I really wanted to believe

1067
01:11:28,918 --> 01:11:30,954
that you were the man
you said you were, but...

1068
01:11:32,589 --> 01:11:34,824
you're full of shit, John.

1069
01:11:39,195 --> 01:11:40,363
[John] Nice to see you.

1070
01:11:40,364 --> 01:11:44,000
[dramatic piano music playing]

1071
01:11:47,471 --> 01:11:49,072
[Sera]
<i>Alyssa was telling the truth.</i>

1072
01:11:52,175 --> 01:11:54,611
<i>But it wasn't sexual harassment.</i>

1073
01:11:56,746 --> 01:11:58,915
<i>It was very consensual.</i>

1074
01:12:01,385 --> 01:12:04,954
You were fucking her
all this time, weren't you?

1075
01:12:10,226 --> 01:12:11,795
<i>And worst of all...</i>

1076
01:12:13,930 --> 01:12:16,566
you were fucking her
on the day we lost our baby.

1077
01:12:25,775 --> 01:12:27,043
[no audible sound]

1078
01:12:29,379 --> 01:12:32,314
[dramatic piano music continues]

1079
01:12:32,315 --> 01:12:34,275
That's why you didn't pick up
the phone, isn't it?

1080
01:12:36,386 --> 01:12:37,954
<i>Isn't it?</i>

1081
01:12:40,289 --> 01:12:41,557
Sera, please.

1082
01:12:41,558 --> 01:12:42,858
I just lied to a fucking cop
for you, John.

1083
01:12:42,859 --> 01:12:44,560
- I didn't ask you to do that.
- No?

1084
01:12:44,561 --> 01:12:47,029
Well, what did you want me to say?
"Oh, I'm-I'm so sorry, officer.

1085
01:12:47,030 --> 01:12:49,064
I have no idea where
my husband was that afternoon."

1086
01:12:49,065 --> 01:12:50,733
Well, you know where I was.
I was running.

1087
01:12:50,734 --> 01:12:52,200
- I told you that.
- You were running?

1088
01:12:52,201 --> 01:12:53,802
- Yeah, I was.
- You were running. No, of course.

1089
01:12:53,803 --> 01:12:55,971
Yes, you were running.
You think they'd buy that?

1090
01:12:55,972 --> 01:12:58,674
I'm trying to protect you.

1091
01:12:58,675 --> 01:13:00,375
I don't wanna have to spend
the next 20 years

1092
01:13:00,376 --> 01:13:03,245
explaining to this baby why their
father's in jail for murder.

1093
01:13:03,246 --> 01:13:06,849
Wait, you don't think I had
anything to do with it, do you?

1094
01:13:06,850 --> 01:13:08,685
Doesn't matter
what I think, John.

1095
01:13:09,586 --> 01:13:11,353
They think you did.

1096
01:13:11,354 --> 01:13:12,856
Ask me.

1097
01:13:14,090 --> 01:13:16,525
- I don't wanna ask you, John.
- Ask me.

1098
01:13:16,526 --> 01:13:19,227
I don't want to ask you.

1099
01:13:19,228 --> 01:13:21,831
[footsteps receding]

1100
01:13:23,199 --> 01:13:26,369
[dramatic instrumental music
