1184
01:18:19,729 --> 01:18:20,930
[sighs]

1185
01:18:21,998 --> 01:18:23,199
[scoffs]

1186
01:18:25,802 --> 01:18:27,102
[John] What are you doing?

1187
01:18:27,103 --> 01:18:30,006
[Sera] I'm painting the nursery,
like we planned.

1188
01:18:31,540 --> 01:18:33,708
[breathes deeply]

1189
01:18:33,709 --> 01:18:35,244
We can't do this anymore.

1190
01:18:37,513 --> 01:18:39,414
Sera.

1191
01:18:39,415 --> 01:18:42,218
We can't. We can't stay here.
We gotta get out.

1192
01:18:44,120 --> 01:18:45,955
Sera, listen to me.

1193
01:18:47,023 --> 01:18:48,223
- I've been a liar.
- John.

1194
01:18:48,224 --> 01:18:49,691
No, no, no. Hear me out.

1195
01:18:49,692 --> 01:18:51,126
I have been a liar

1196
01:18:51,127 --> 01:18:53,128
and a shitty fucking husband,

1197
01:18:53,129 --> 01:18:55,663
and I hope to God
one day, you can forgive me.

1198
01:18:55,664 --> 01:18:56,665
Please.

1199
01:18:57,867 --> 01:18:59,068
I don't care.

1200
01:19:00,036 --> 01:19:01,870
I don't care, John.

1201
01:19:01,871 --> 01:19:04,707
I'm trying to protect our life.

1202
01:19:06,943 --> 01:19:08,411
The one we deserve.

1203
01:19:09,212 --> 01:19:10,579
The one we agreed to.

1204
01:19:12,181 --> 01:19:14,316
The one we always dreamed of.

1205
01:19:14,317 --> 01:19:17,152
Look at you. Look at you.

1206
01:19:17,153 --> 01:19:18,754
You're just covering it all up.

1207
01:19:19,655 --> 01:19:20,956
I mean, don't you see?

1208
01:19:20,957 --> 01:19:22,657
It doesn't matter what shade
of green you paint the nursery.

1209
01:19:22,658 --> 01:19:25,894
This house will always be
what it is. A fucking cage.

1210
01:19:25,895 --> 01:19:28,231
- It ends right now.
- No.

1211
01:19:29,999 --> 01:19:31,033
John.

1212
01:19:31,034 --> 01:19:33,369
[dramatic violin music plays]

1213
01:19:35,104 --> 01:19:37,973
- No. No, John, stop!
- [chains clanging]

1214
01:19:37,974 --> 01:19:40,375
John, please stop.
You'll ruin everything.

1215
01:19:40,376 --> 01:19:42,510
John, just stop.
Just listen to me.

1216
01:19:42,511 --> 01:19:43,745
Stop!

1217
01:19:43,746 --> 01:19:46,281
Enough!
Enough! It's done!

1218
01:19:46,282 --> 01:19:49,852
- Enough. I'm opening this fucking door.
- No.

1219
01:19:49,853 --> 01:19:53,789
- No. Stop it, John!
- [panting]

1220
01:19:55,758 --> 01:19:56,758
[Sera grunts]

1221
01:20:02,531 --> 01:20:04,733
[footsteps]

1222
01:20:07,036 --> 01:20:10,039
[John breathing heavily]

1223
01:20:17,813 --> 01:20:19,082
[John groans]

1224
01:20:26,422 --> 01:20:27,422
What?

1225
01:20:29,258 --> 01:20:31,527
I couldn't let you open it,
John.

1226
01:20:32,628 --> 01:20:33,628
Sera.

1227
01:20:35,164 --> 01:20:36,199
[Sera] You know that.

1228
01:20:37,166 --> 01:20:40,803
When you open a door, you have to
be prepared for what you might find.

1229
01:20:49,112 --> 01:20:50,379
[phone rings]

1230
01:20:50,914 --> 01:20:52,781
[ominous music plays]

1231
01:20:54,483 --> 01:20:55,483
Alyssa.

1232
01:20:57,286 --> 01:20:58,554
What did you do?

1233
01:20:59,989 --> 01:21:01,857
She came to the house that day.

1234
01:21:08,164 --> 01:21:10,699
[grunts, sighs]

1235
01:21:11,234 --> 01:21:12,701
[door thuds]

1236
01:21:17,773 --> 01:21:19,108
[sighs]

1237
01:21:21,177 --> 01:21:22,678
[creaks]

1238
01:21:25,148 --> 01:21:27,516
[footsteps]

1239
01:21:31,187 --> 01:21:33,789
[ominous music continues]

1240
01:21:54,577 --> 01:21:56,345
[Sera] Get out of my house.

1241
01:22:00,916 --> 01:22:01,916
No.

1242
01:22:04,653 --> 01:22:07,156
All of this
was supposed to be mine.

1243
01:22:07,856 --> 01:22:08,856
Get out.

1244
01:22:10,159 --> 01:22:12,394
You don't deserve this.

1245
01:22:12,395 --> 01:22:14,697
You're fucking crazy.

1246
01:22:16,432 --> 01:22:18,667
You don't deserve this.

1247
01:22:21,804 --> 01:22:24,206
Ah! [panting]

1248
01:22:24,207 --> 01:22:25,707
- [grunts]
- [body thuds]

1249
01:22:25,708 --> 01:22:28,411
[panting]

1250
01:22:29,878 --> 01:22:33,982
[grunting, whimpering]

1251
01:22:33,983 --> 01:22:35,317
Help me.

1252
01:22:35,318 --> 01:22:39,522
I was defending myself
and our unborn child.

1253
01:22:42,558 --> 01:22:45,627
I started to call the police,
but there was too much at risk.

1254
01:22:45,628 --> 01:22:48,530
[breathes heavily, sniffles]

1255
01:22:48,531 --> 01:22:50,765
<i>And no one I could trust.</i>

1256
01:22:50,766 --> 01:22:51,967
Help me.

1257
01:22:54,870 --> 01:22:57,540
[whimpering]

1258
01:22:59,175 --> 01:23:02,710
- Please. - [Sera] <i>Our
perfect life was at stake.</i>

1259
01:23:02,711 --> 01:23:05,780
Help me. Please.

1260
01:23:05,781 --> 01:23:07,350
I knew what I had to do.

1261
01:23:09,285 --> 01:23:11,186
[Alyssa gasps]

1262
01:23:11,187 --> 01:23:13,988
[dark music plays]

1263
01:23:13,989 --> 01:23:15,324
[grunts]

1264
01:23:19,228 --> 01:23:20,896
[Alyssa grunts]

1265
01:23:26,302 --> 01:23:29,572
- [music fades]
- [Sera breathing heavily]

1266
01:23:35,144 --> 01:23:36,978
[Sera]
<i>I needed to clear my head.</i>

1267
01:23:36,979 --> 01:23:40,014
[piano playing]

1268
01:23:40,015 --> 01:23:41,717
<i>To find a path forward.</i>

1269
01:23:45,221 --> 01:23:46,789
<i>I weighed my options,</i>

1270
01:23:47,523 --> 01:23:49,858
<i>considered the causes
and effects.</i>

1271
01:23:51,727 --> 01:23:55,698
<i>And from the chaos, clarity.</i>

1272
01:24:06,309 --> 01:24:08,711
[piano continues playing]

1273
01:24:26,162 --> 01:24:27,563
[Sera exhales]

1274
01:24:47,716 --> 01:24:49,585
Alyssa. She just left
my fucking house.

1275
01:24:52,221 --> 01:24:53,722
You were driving her car.

1276
01:24:57,960 --> 01:25:00,027
[tense music plays]

1277
01:25:00,028 --> 01:25:01,630
I couldn't just leave it here.

1278
01:25:02,331 --> 01:25:04,600
[revving]

1279
01:25:07,470 --> 01:25:09,605
<i>I managed to lose you
at the turn.</i>

1280
01:25:17,380 --> 01:25:18,947
Come on, come on, come on.

1281
01:25:20,916 --> 01:25:23,886
I abandoned it where
no one would find the body.

1282
01:25:29,124 --> 01:25:31,659
<i>And then I took her phone,</i>

1283
01:25:31,660 --> 01:25:33,962
<i>and I uploaded
a few last pictures.</i>

1284
01:25:35,898 --> 01:25:36,898
[water sloshes]

1285
01:25:40,236 --> 01:25:43,539
And I emailed the firm
asking for some time off.

1286
01:25:45,174 --> 01:25:46,575
"Self-care," they say.

1287
01:25:49,612 --> 01:25:51,680
[Sera] <i>I got rid of my clothes.</i>

1288
01:25:54,783 --> 01:25:56,985
<i>It was all going perfectly.</i>

1289
01:25:58,721 --> 01:26:01,123
<i>Until somehow, I missed.</i>

1290
01:26:01,890 --> 01:26:03,291
<i>One bullet.</i>

1291
01:26:03,292 --> 01:26:05,460
- What the hell is that? - [Sera]
R<i>ight through the painting.</i>

1292
01:26:05,461 --> 01:26:07,395
<i>It was easy
to predict your reaction.</i>

1293
01:26:07,396 --> 01:26:09,297
[John] <i>There is a bullet
in our wall.</i>

1294
01:26:09,298 --> 01:26:12,300
[Sera] <i>Because there's probably
a rational explanation.</i>

1295
01:26:12,301 --> 01:26:14,336
Please, drop it.

1296
01:26:14,337 --> 01:26:15,403
<i>Or so I thought.</i>

1297
01:26:15,404 --> 01:26:16,638
No!

1298
01:26:16,639 --> 01:26:17,872
<i>You just couldn't
leave it alone.</i>

1299
01:26:17,873 --> 01:26:18,941
[Sera grunts]

1300
01:26:30,253 --> 01:26:31,453
So, now, you know the truth.

1301
01:26:31,454 --> 01:26:32,688
[John exhales]

1302
01:26:40,162 --> 01:26:42,731
We're gonna get you
a really good lawyer.

1303
01:26:48,837 --> 01:26:50,072
Hey, John.

1304
01:26:51,374 --> 01:26:52,575
[gun cocks]

1305
01:26:55,177 --> 01:26:57,579
[ominous music plays]

1306
01:26:57,580 --> 01:26:59,515
Don't be stupid.

1307
01:27:00,283 --> 01:27:01,484
You don't get it, do you?

1308
01:27:02,117 --> 01:27:05,854
If you make that call, you'll be
going to jail for murder, not me.

1309
01:27:06,889 --> 01:27:08,090
Sit.

1310
01:27:11,226 --> 01:27:12,260
Sit!

1311
01:27:12,261 --> 01:27:14,196
[John exhales sharply]

1312
01:27:18,801 --> 01:27:21,970
Okay, okay, okay, okay.

1313
01:27:27,376 --> 01:27:29,545
You're not seeing
the full picture.

1314
01:27:30,313 --> 01:27:32,781
You lured her to our house,

1315
01:27:34,116 --> 01:27:36,784
you murdered her,

1316
01:27:36,785 --> 01:27:38,753
<i>and then you hid her body
under the stairs.</i>

1317
01:27:38,754 --> 01:27:41,757
<i>You even nailed it shut
so that no one would find her.</i>

1318
01:27:48,196 --> 01:27:52,199
I had no idea until the police
started snooping around.

1319
01:27:52,200 --> 01:27:55,103
[ominous music continues]

1320
01:27:58,674 --> 01:28:00,743
And then I found
that phone of hers you kept.

1321
01:28:04,613 --> 01:28:06,649
And I put the pieces together.

1322
01:28:08,050 --> 01:28:10,819
I realized
you killed that poor girl.

1323
01:28:13,622 --> 01:28:15,657
When I confronted you,
you attacked me,

1324
01:28:15,658 --> 01:28:17,926
and I was forced
to do the unthinkable.

1325
01:28:20,062 --> 01:28:22,464
I shot my husband
in self-defense.

1326
01:28:22,465 --> 01:28:23,732
[John scoffs]

1327
01:28:25,734 --> 01:28:28,571
When the police arrive,
they find me hysterical.

1328
01:28:29,372 --> 01:28:30,572
I tell them everything I know.

1329
01:28:30,573 --> 01:28:32,675
I lead them to Alyssa's body.
"It's...

1330
01:28:33,976 --> 01:28:36,011
a terrible tragedy,"
they all say.

1331
01:28:37,346 --> 01:28:40,114
And then I raise our baby

1332
01:28:40,115 --> 01:28:44,186
in the house
we always dreamed of by myself.

1333
01:28:45,854 --> 01:28:49,558
Or you say nothing.

1334
01:28:50,759 --> 01:28:52,528
Nobody's the wiser.

1335
01:28:53,228 --> 01:28:57,800
We stay in this home, our baby
on the way, our promise kept.

1336
01:29:06,675 --> 01:29:07,910
What about Alyssa?

1337
01:29:09,912 --> 01:29:12,247
A tragic disappearance.

1338
01:29:13,348 --> 01:29:14,950
Most likely suicide.

1339
01:29:17,786 --> 01:29:20,055
Whatever the case,
we'll weather the storm.

1340
01:29:21,990 --> 01:29:23,859
We'll survive this together.

1341
01:29:25,628 --> 01:29:27,195
Or I'll survive it alone.

1342
01:29:30,566 --> 01:29:32,667
There's only one answer, John.

1343
01:29:32,668 --> 01:29:34,737
But the choice is yours.

1344
01:29:37,440 --> 01:29:38,741
What's it gonna be?

1345
01:29:43,078 --> 01:29:44,379
[music fades]

1346
01:29:46,281 --> 01:29:49,217
[piano music plays]

1347
01:30:02,364 --> 01:30:04,867
[indistinct chattering]

1348
01:30:08,036 --> 01:30:11,639
[Kathryn] Oh, my God,
look at this. It's so cute.

1349
01:30:11,640 --> 01:30:13,941
St... A little baby.
Are we dying? I'm...

1350
01:30:13,942 --> 01:30:16,410
You know, old friend,
I'm proud of you.

1351
01:30:16,411 --> 01:30:17,546
You had a hell of a year.

1352
01:30:18,180 --> 01:30:20,314
But you-you came through
to the other side.

1353
01:30:20,315 --> 01:30:21,649
[soft chuckle]

1354
01:30:21,650 --> 01:30:22,950
- Oh, pictures. We haven't done pictures.
- Oh, yes!

1355
01:30:22,951 --> 01:30:24,652
Everybody up, everybody up.

1356
01:30:24,653 --> 01:30:26,087
By the way, you ever, uh,

1357
01:30:26,088 --> 01:30:27,890
you ever find out
what was in the cellar?

1358
01:30:29,424 --> 01:30:31,626
Oh, yeah, that's where
all the bodies are buried.

1359
01:30:31,627 --> 01:30:34,161
[Steven chuckles]

1360
01:30:34,162 --> 01:30:36,330
Hey, everybody,
let's get pictures.

1361
01:30:36,331 --> 01:30:38,333
Everybody in. Come on.

1362
01:30:41,504 --> 01:30:42,770
- Sera, I almost forgot.
- Yeah?

1363
01:30:42,771 --> 01:30:44,539
Some guy dropped off
a gift for you.

1364
01:30:44,540 --> 01:30:46,308
- It's on the piano. Mm.
- Oh, thank you.

1365
01:30:49,845 --> 01:30:51,078
Why are you being
such a sourpuss?

1366
01:30:51,079 --> 01:30:52,747
I'm sorry.
No, no, I'm good, I'm good.

1367
01:30:52,748 --> 01:30:54,181
Smile, okay?

1368
01:30:54,182 --> 01:30:55,717
- Yeah, I'm happy.
- Cheer up.

1369
01:30:55,718 --> 01:30:57,619
Baby, there's something here
for us.

1370
01:30:57,620 --> 01:30:59,787
[Kathryn] And if we could have all the
attractive people up front, please,

1371
01:30:59,788 --> 01:31:01,222
that would be great.

1372
01:31:01,223 --> 01:31:02,157
Here we go, lining up.

1373
01:31:02,158 --> 01:31:04,391
Oh, my God, look at this group.

1374
01:31:04,392 --> 01:31:06,228
[John exhales]

1375
01:31:13,602 --> 01:31:14,837
"Dear John and Sera..."

1376
01:31:15,904 --> 01:31:18,106
[Emmett]
<i>Congratulations to you both.</i>

1377
01:31:18,907 --> 01:31:21,843
<i>I hope this wonderful news
helps to realize</i>

1378
01:31:21,844 --> 01:31:23,445
<i>the ideal life you were seeking.</i>

1379
01:31:24,713 --> 01:31:25,880
<i>By starting a family,</i>

1380
01:31:25,881 --> 01:31:27,849
<i>you have transformed this house</i>

1381
01:31:27,850 --> 01:31:30,117
<i>back into a home again.</i>

1382
01:31:30,118 --> 01:31:31,887
<i>For this,
I am eternally grateful.</i>

1383
01:31:32,655 --> 01:31:36,758
<i>I understand you both faced many
challenges to make this happen.</i>

1384
01:31:36,759 --> 01:31:39,561
<i>I trust it's all been worth it.</i>

1385
01:31:39,562 --> 01:31:42,731
<i>My gift to you is the key
to the cellar door.</i>

1386
01:31:43,666 --> 01:31:47,468
<i>Whether you choose to use it
is entirely up to you.</i>

1387
01:31:47,469 --> 01:31:50,772
<i>But I believe you already know
what's inside.</i>

1388
01:31:50,773 --> 01:31:52,306
<i>Wishing you both the best</i>

1389
01:31:52,307 --> 01:31:55,543
<i>as you continue to write
new chapters in your life.</i>

1390
01:31:55,544 --> 01:31:58,180
<i>Sincerely, Emmett.</i>

1391
01:31:59,682 --> 01:32:02,850
Oh, you two,
get in here for photos.

1392
01:32:02,851 --> 01:32:05,252
Oh, my God. [laughs]
I know what they were doing.

1393
01:32:05,253 --> 01:32:07,856
- [Sera laughs]
- Okay, get in the photo.

1394
01:32:09,725 --> 01:32:11,392
Perfect.

1395
01:32:11,393 --> 01:32:12,560
That looks great.

1396
01:32:12,561 --> 01:32:14,495
Okay, here we go.

1397
01:32:14,496 --> 01:32:15,931
And...

1398
01:32:16,865 --> 01:32:17,899
happy, happy.

1399
01:32:17,900 --> 01:32:20,367
Big smiles. Cheese!

1400
01:32:20,368 --> 01:32:21,636
[camera shutter clicks]

1401
01:32:21,637 --> 01:32:25,173
I'm dying. I'm dying. Okay.
[speaking indistinctly]

1402
01:32:26,909 --> 01:32:28,209
Yes, yes, yes, okay.

1403
01:32:28,210 --> 01:32:30,745
Everybody in, everybody in.

1404
01:32:30,746 --> 01:32:33,949
[dramatic instrumental music
playing]

1405
01:32:59,975 --> 01:33:03,145
[dramatic instrumental music
continues]

1406
01:33:13,689 --> 01:33:15,190
[music ends]

1407
01:33:16,892 --> 01:33:20,062
[piano music plays]

1408
01:34:29,331 --> 01:34:30,632
[music ends]

1409
01:34:31,800 --> 01:34:34,970
[instrumental music plays]

1410
01:35:33,929 --> 01:35:35,597
[music ends]

1411
01:35:39,301 --> 01:35:42,470
[light instrumental music plays]

1412
01:37:03,818 --> 01:37:05,487
[music ends]